# vLLM v0.26.0 patch 03/18 (apply after the four DeepSeek-V4 patches above it).
#
# DeepSeek-V4 on ROCm: batch-invariant indexer top-k as one deterministic kernel.
#
# Under VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1 the indexer selects its top-k (prefill chunks and
# sparse decode) with _dsv4_det_topk_kernel: the index_topk largest scores
# under the fp32 bit order, ties to the larger column, ascending row-local
# indices. Includes a tidy-up of the sparse-decode code (line lengths,
# docstrings, int32 seq_lens).
#
# Why BI needs it: top_k_per_row_prefill's output order is not fixed run to run
# and its candidate at the cutoff depends on the launch shape; sparse attention
# sums in index order, so both change bits.
#
# Upstream: not yet proposed (same DeepSeek-V4 ROCm RFC as patch 02).
#
# Source commits:
#   [ROCm][DSv4] Batch-invariant indexer top-k as one deterministic kernel
#   [ROCm][DSv4] Sparse decode: tidy (line lengths, docstrings, int32 seq_lens)
#
